# Design Anti-Patterns

## Stop and Fix

- **AP-01** Circular buttons must be fixed square + radius = size/2 (no HUG/AUTO)
- **AP-02** Exactly 1 accent color for primary actions; hierarchy via filled/outlined/ghost, not more colors
- **AP-03** One padding value for same-type cards; 8px grid only
- **AP-04** Max 2 border-radius values + pill across the product
- **AP-05** Body ≥16px; weight ≥400 below 18px; contrast ≥4.5:1; no weight 300 below 18px
- **AP-06** Only 1 filled primary CTA per screen
- **AP-07** Mobile primary CTA in bottom half (thumb zone)
- **AP-08** Labels = verb + noun (`Save Draft`), never OK/Yes/Submit/Confirm alone
- **AP-09** Feedback ≤100ms; loading state if >400ms
- **AP-10** Modals need ≥2 close paths (X + overlay / swipe)
- **AP-14** Nav icons need text labels
- **AP-15** Transitions ~300ms, gentle easing; no bounce in professional UIs
- **AP-16** ≥3 text sizes for hierarchy (e.g. 24 / 18 / 16 / 12)
- **AP-17** Cards: max 3–4 lines; link to detail

## Dark Patterns — Never

Confirm-shaming, buried deletion, hidden costs, forced continuity, trick questions, first-use overload, settings graveyard, notification spam, choice overload (>3–4), fake scarcity / pre-checked upsells.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] One primary filled CTA
- [ ] Circular buttons actually circular
- [ ] One accent color
- [ ] Consistent radius / card padding
- [ ] Clear type hierarchy (3+ sizes)
- [ ] Mobile CTA in thumb zone
- [ ] Verb + noun labels
- [ ] Loading for slow actions
- [ ] Modals closable 2+ ways
